## TRAPS. EVERY ONE OF THESE COST TIME TODAY

1. **`legal/` is digest-locked.** `apps/bff/test/integration/legal-versions.test.ts`
   recomputes the sha256 of every file under `legal/` and fails on drift. Editing
   a legal document REQUIRES updating the registry in
   `apps/bff/src/lib/legal-documents.ts` and deciding whether the change is
   material. **That failure is the control working. Never change a recorded
   digest, version or epoch to make a test pass.**
2. **`ignore_changes = [image, user_data]`** on `module.compute.hcloud_server`.
   A plain `terraform apply` will NOT pick up a cloud-init change, and an apply
   without `TF_VAR_tailscale_auth_key` renders an empty key, producing a node with
   no Tailscale and **no public SSH**, i.e. unreachable. Use
   `terraform apply -replace='module.compute.hcloud_server.app[0]'` (quote it, zsh
   globs brackets) with a freshly minted key.
3. **`-var` overrides do not persist.** `terraform.tfvars` is gitignored and holds
   `location = "ash"`, `app_server_type = "cpx21"`. A migration applied only via
   command-line flags is not migrated, it is temporarily disguised.
4. **Neon's PROXY, not just its pooler, discards libpq startup parameters.** The
   pool options in `lib/db.ts` have no effect in any deployed environment. The
   role default is the entire control. `PGOPTIONS` is refused on both endpoints.
5. **`pullfm_app` can delete its own query ceiling.** `ALTER ROLE self SET
   statement_timeout = 0` succeeds; `statement_timeout` is a `USERSET` GUC. T10's
   only mitigation is self-revocable, and the periodic verifier is the only thing
   that would notice.
6. **Do not cap `logical_size_bytes`.** It bounds a single branch for that
   branch's LIFETIME, not per period, and the canonical loader is stage-then-swap
   so staging peaks near 22 GB during a load. A validation block now rejects any
   value between 1 and 25 GB. Also: **never set `suspend_timeout_seconds = -1`**,
   because an always-warm 0.25 CU compute is 186 of the 200 CU-hour cap.
7. **The private NIC boot race self-heals now**, but if you see Redis failing to
   bind `10.20.1.11`, check `ip -4 -br addr` and `/var/lib/pullfm/private-net-FAILED`.
8. **A container reporting `healthy` says nothing about published ports.** The
   Redis healthcheck runs `redis-cli ping` inside the container over its own
   loopback. Check `docker ps --format '{{.Ports}}'` and TCP-connect from the host.
9. **`schema: { hide: true }` silently removes a route from the authorization test
   chain.** There is a reconciliation test and `security/zap/upstream-scope.tsv`
   that fail by design on an unclassified route. Do not silence them.
10. **`fast-json-stringify` silently deletes response members** not declared in
    the schema. Declare everything you return.
11. **Vault items are addressed BY TITLE, not by item id.** `tools/check-public-identifiers.mjs`
    treats an item id as a direct object reference. Only the `op://` reference
    syntax rejects parentheses; `op item get "Title"` handles them.

